;; fault-ld-x0-fault.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-ld-x0-fault.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-ld-x0-fault.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "fault-ld-x0-fault.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-ld-x0-fault.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). D-LOAD-X0 one failure mode over: the access fault fires even with rd = x0. The address" "is outside BOTH reference platforms' maps, so the guest runs cross-model.")
(expectations (program "fault-ld-x0-fault.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (step (n 0) (insn "lui x11, 0x40000") (writes (write (reg "x11") (value "0x0000000040000000"))) (derivation "0x40000 << 12 = 0x40000000; bit 31 is clear, so the sign extension adds nothing. The address is outside sail-riscv's MainMemory region, outside spike's DRAM, and no device on either platform.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC)")) (step (n 1) (insn "ld x0, x11, 0") (writes) (derivation "The effective address 0x40000000 is outside every declared region, so the load raises an access-fault exception — and D-LOAD-X0 says the discarded destination suppresses NOTHING: the fault fires exactly as if rd were an ordinary register. No register is written. Measured on both references: cause 0x05, tval 0x0000000040000000.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (D-LOAD-X0); RVI-RV64I §3.1.3 + RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (D-ADDRESS-SPACE)")))
